<section class="band" id="start">
  <div class="wrap start">
    <div class="start__text" data-reveal>
      <h2>Get started</h2>
      <p class="lead">HoloTouch runs on a laptop CPU with an ordinary webcam.</p>
      <h3>What it needs</h3>
      <ul class="needs">
        <li>Linux with an X11 session, xfwm4 and a running compositor</li>
        <li>A webcam</li>
        <li>Python 3.12</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="fine">A few tools are optional, each for one feature: smooth scrolling, volume, dictation and the rest. <code>holotouch doctor</code> reports which are present.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="start__side" data-reveal>
      <div class="term">
        <div class="term__bar">
          <span>Terminal</span>
          <button type="button" class="term__copy" id="copy">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <pre id="commands"><span class="term__p">$</span> git clone https://github.com/justanotherinternetguy/HoloTouch
<span class="term__p">$</span> cd HoloTouch
<span class="term__p">$</span> uv sync
<span class="term__p">$</span> uv run holotouch doctor
<span class="term__p">$</span> uv run holotouch panel</pre>
      </div>
      <dl class="commands">
        <div><dt><code>holotouch panel</code></dt><dd>Open the control panel: start and stop, the gesture guide, and practice.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><code>holotouch run</code></dt><dd>Start tracking and the overlay.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><code>holotouch run --dry-run</code></dt><dd>Practice on two stand-in windows. Your real ones are left alone.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><code>holotouch doctor</code></dt><dd>Check the machine, and measure the tracking rate.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
